9 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1031 "Factoring Linear Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1033 87 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7f29909c-8f45-5a17-820a-13a0a327cd5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096445 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4279" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096445 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$. Given that $7\\mathbf{a}+14\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\lambda \\left(3\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b} \\right)$ are equal vectors, find the scalar factor $\\lambda$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096445 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "069b2882-f4a9-589f-a903-4e89d077cd85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096445 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\n7\\mathbf{a}+14\\mathbf{b}= \\dfrac{7}{3} (3\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=\\dfrac{7}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096446 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4280" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096446 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $\\mathbf a$ is shown in the diagram below. Draw the vectors $2\\mathbf a$ and $-3\\mathbf a$.\n\n![](images/a5/a5eaa8baaf303ecbfa6c0fb207d6b19836cc90fc331e238cd473109f44fddf80.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096446 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1329498-4413-5d87-a814-be0d57a3afd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096446 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that both $2\\mathbf{a}$ and $-3\\mathbf{a}$ must be parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nNow, for the vector $2\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $2\\mathbf{a}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $2\\mathbf{a}$ have the same direction since the factor $2$ is positive.\n\n![](images/41/41eba7e6c5bbe420418726bd45efa668dc6be5ff5144ba35d52b53a43925c333.png)\n\nNext, for the vector $-3\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $3\\mathbf{a}$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $-3\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions since the factor $-3$ is negative.\n\n![](images/ed/eda3f2572d98ef1789292ec6d35569487b32efa459673dcb95f8fdd0d1f4ae5b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096494 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5183" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096494 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the diagram that is shown below. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\mathbf{b}=-\\mathbf{c}$\n2. $\\mathbf{e}=2\\mathbf{a}$\n3. $\\mathbf{a}=2\\mathbf{e}$\n\n![](images/95/95ae711c1ccbf7543e6d269aa8d817a66e2ac348113ea71f3a1babcbb23d1ca3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096494 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "11c09a26-0e83-5a77-b777-aea8a3594960" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096494 #edb/ref 1074 "- Statement I is false. The vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ have different magnitudes. So, $\\mathbf{b} \\neq -\\mathbf{c}$.\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{e}$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{e}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Statement III is false. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$ is greater than the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq 2\\mathbf{e}$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504745 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504750 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504753 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504768 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504773 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504780 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504802 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504803 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504821 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504832 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504834 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504837 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504838 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504839 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504841 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186572160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186572164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining Whether Two Vectors are Parallel" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186504848 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096648 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "27d5c96d-ca13-5c1e-83d3-0dc9f6da0f83" #edb/ref 17