e diagram above shows the vector $a$. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $4a$?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504021 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd1fd2b2-3e3c-5f17-91c5-e33207e2fa01" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504021 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that $4a$ must be parallel to $a$.\n\nNow, for the vector $4a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $4a$ is $4$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $4a$ have the same direction since the factor $4$ is positive.\n\nThe required vectors are shown below.\n\n![](images/4f/4fd95161ecee991b1d7b8c3ef3510010915bd08a4126719b8a750b93b51d0032.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504023 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186096649.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504023 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "3b8d388a-714a-55a4-8f2e-330d279175ef" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504745 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504766 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504745 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504745 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $λ(5a - 25b)$ and $6a - 30b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504745 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0803379b-a2dd-51ec-9c3c-dfbd721fe7b8" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504745 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(5a - 25b)=λ(5)a+λ(-25)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{6}{5} = \\frac{6}{5} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-30}{-25} = \\frac{6}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n6a - 30b=\\frac{6}{5}(5a - 25b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504750 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504796 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504750 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504750 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $-8a - 10b$ and $λ(20a + 25b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504750 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0ecb5994-c9d9-519e-8505-fb41a7d19179" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504750 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(20a + 25b)=λ(20)a+λ(25)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-8}{20} = -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-10}{25} = -\\frac{2}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-8a - 10b=-\\frac{2}{5}(20a + 25b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504753 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504791 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504753 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504753 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $-3a - 24b$ and $λ(0.5a + 4b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504753 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "14ea91d3-f94c-5dd9-b51c-cb8c953c07f2" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504753 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{2}a + 4b)=λ(\\frac{1}{2})a+λ(4)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-3}{\\frac{1}{2}} = -6 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-24}{4} = -6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-3a - 24b=-6(\\frac{1}{2}a + 4b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-6\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504768 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504799 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504768 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504768 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $λ(0.25a - 3b)$ and $-a + 12b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504768 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "281e43ed-d77f-5100-ba06-3efb56464379" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504768 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{4}a - 3b)=λ(\\frac{1}{4})a+λ(-3)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-1}{\\frac{1}{4}} = -4 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{12}{-3} = -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-a + 12b=-4(\\frac{1}{4}a - 3b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-4\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504773 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504810 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504773 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504773 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $18a + 45b$ and $λ(4a + 10b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504773 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "315d6a79-c820-530f-a728-86a6ee67757a" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504773 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(4a + 10b)=λ(4)a+λ(10)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{18}{4} = \\frac{9}{2} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{45}{10} = \\frac{9}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n18a + 45b=\\frac{9}{2}(4a + 10b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=\\frac{9}{2}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504780 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504818 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504780 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504780 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $-16a - 12b$ and $λ(20a + 15b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504780 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40a6d99d-54df-5f7a-8a53-416c89a4a6f9" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504780 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(20a + 15b)=λ(20)a+λ(15)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-16}{20} = -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-12}{15} = -\\frac{4}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-16a - 12b=-\\frac{4}{5}(20a + 15b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-\\frac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504802 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504765 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504802 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504802 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $λ(3a + 4b)$ and $12a + 16b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504802 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "88ca6c0b-f159-58fc-adb2-cf4950ce3bfd" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504802 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(3a + 4b)=λ(3)a+λ(4)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{12}{3} = 4 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{16}{4} = 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n12a + 16b=4(3a + 4b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=4\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504803 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504782 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504803 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504803 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $λ(3a - 4b)$ and $18a - 24b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504803 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a8aa6aa-79a2-59ee-8afa-533036e8e56c" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504803 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(3a - 4b)=λ(3)a+λ(-4)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{18}{3} = 6 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-24}{-4} = 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n18a - 24b=6(3a - 4b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=6\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504821 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504811 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504821 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504821 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $24a - 8b$ and $λ(3a - b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504821 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c06fdca4-9c0f-5aba-ba3a-3f0cefff0623" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504821 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(3a - b)=λ(3)a+λ(-1)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{24}{3} = 8 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-8}{-1} = 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n24a - 8b=8(3a - b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=8\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504832 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504833 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504832 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504832 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $λ(0.5a + 3b)$ and $-a - 6b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504832 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e813b171-b626-57db-af36-b0b2e170a174" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504832 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{2}a + 3b)=λ(\\frac{1}{2})a+λ(3)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-1}{\\frac{1}{2}} = -2 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-6}{3} = -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-a - 6b=-2(\\frac{1}{2}a + 3b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-2\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504834 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504767 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504834 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504834 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $4a - 8b$ and $λ(a - 2b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504834 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eb65d9fd-5b96-51a4-9bed-d3ab5895f629" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504834 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(a - 2b)=λ(1)a+λ(-2)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{4}{1} = 4 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-8}{-2} = 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n4a - 8b=4(a - 2b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=4\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504837 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504835 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504837 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504837 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $λ(3a + 12b)$ and $-5a - 20b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504837 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f051a23b-4fb5-55c6-8552-3b7f053713a4" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504837 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(3a + 12b)=λ(3)a+λ(12)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-5}{3} = -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-20}{12} = -\\frac{5}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-5a - 20b=-\\frac{5}{3}(3a + 12b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-\\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504838 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504762 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504838 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504838 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $3a + 24b$ and $λ(0.5a + 4b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504838 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0dc3593-c754-5805-816a-41c4fccabc8f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504838 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{2}a + 4b)=λ(\\frac{1}{2})a+λ(4)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{3}{\\frac{1}{2}} = 6 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{24}{4} = 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n3a + 24b=6(\\frac{1}{2}a + 4b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=6\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504839 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504769 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504839 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504839 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $-a - 2b$ and $λ(0.5a + b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504839 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0e435c8-cd66-5b3b-b59e-c0b5f48a6d99" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504839 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{2}a + b)=λ(\\frac{1}{2})a+λ(1)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-1}{\\frac{1}{2}} = -2 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-2}{1} = -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-a - 2b=-2(\\frac{1}{2}a + b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-2\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504841 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186504843 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186504841 #edb/r